{
  "note": "The config of the look harness (tools/look/look.mjs). A selector is \"the hook, or the old selector\". idsMayGo and classesMayGo are the standing lists of the contract: a lost id or class of a list gives a warning only, and each other lost id or class fails. An entry of classesMayGo can end with *. The list changes holds each change that a row asks for. Each entry names its row, the pages it holds for (each page when it names none) and what it allows; the header of look.mjs says what each key allows. An id, a word or a control that is gone or new, and that no entry allows, fails. The counts of a word are the counts of the build of 49d3ba0 (the state before Wave 2c) and of the build of each row. In the pages drill and signals the step learnCards presses the control of each learn card of the Drill that shows (2c-plan C11, ruling LEARN-GAP); with no learn card it presses nothing. The page drill-learn shows the first screen of the Drill with no press: with the learn card of job U1-D it shows the card, and before that job it shows the first question. The page yard names its text mirror (ruling LOOK-MIRROR): the mirror must be in the page, with one line for the engine and one line for each of the six tracks. A build job does not edit this file.",
